  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The leading open-source toolkit for image-guided therapy research built on 3D Slicer. BSD-3-Clause licence, 110 stars, actively maintained (April 2026). Developed by PerkLab (Queen's University), a globally recognised group in surgical navigation and IGT research. Integrates with tracking hardware via OpenIGTLink and supports real-time needle, catheter, and instrument guidance workflows. Niche but authoritative for teams building intraoperative navigation or ultrasound-guided intervention pipelines; requires 3D Slicer as a runtime dependency.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-12",
